{
  "id": "Compound::DB01628 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Etoricoxib, a selective COX-2 inhibitor, is shown to bind to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with all three paths indicating that Cyp2c19 participates in the activity of limonene monooxygenase, a key enzyme in the oxidation of limonene. The shared involvement of Cyp2c19 in this metabolic pathway suggests a potential mechanism by which Etoricoxib may influence the metabolism of limonene, potentially affecting its bioavailability or efficacy. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores supports a robust, mechanistically coherent relationship between Etoricoxib and Cyp2c9, as all pathways converge on the same core mechanism involving Cyp2c19 and its role in limonene monooxygenase activity. The integration of these evidence points reinforces the hypothesis that Etoricoxib may modulate Cyp2c9 activity through its interaction with Cyp2c19, thereby influencing the metabolic processing of substrates that are substrates of this enzyme.",
